<title>USA: Wall Street opens lower.</title>
<headline>Wall Street opens lower.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Dow industrials and the Nasdaq compasite opened lower on Friday, after stronger-than-expected housing starts. Hewlett-Packard Co shares were not immediately open after trading down in pre-open on soft earnings.</p>
<p>--Dow Industrials off 22.26 at 7311.29.</p>
<p>--Nasdaq Composite off 5.59 at 1347.99.</p>
<p>--S&amp;P Index off 2.10 at 839.78.</p>
<p>--NYSE advance/decline 587/561</p>
<p>--Nasdaq advance/decline 852/856</p>
<p>--The 30-year long bond off 6/32 to yield 6.88 percent.</p>
<p>-- Wall Street desk, 212-859-1737</p>
</text>
